\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 STEP-BY-STEP BEATS\
\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 1. Establish the platform: raised in front of the engineering tower (there for sound/lighting/production coordination \'97 established-facts.md, \'93Rock Against Revival (the festival)\'94). Two thrones for Holy Momma (Sarah) and Great Teacher (Chanta); seats for Aunt Kathy and Aunt Hayley. Kathy and Hayley are a couple, together since \'93After the Barbecue\'94 (Scrivener UUID 744254E7-E892-4F08-B1A0-CD04CB20A087, Second Draft status) \'97 verified directly against that scene\'92s prose. A look passing between them across the platform\'92s chaos is confirmed canon (tagged so in the old Document Notes for this chapter\'92s prior draft), not an invented beat; play it as a single, unremarked glance rather than any on-page discussion of the relationship \'97 this is atmosphere, not a scene about them. Staging/regalia DNA from \'93The Inauguration of the High Elvis\'94 (content.rtf, UUID B70CFF1A) \'97 burlesque-grand thrones, over-the-top regalia, the established liturgy \'93Praise the Dawkins! Bless the Holy Momma!\'94 and the \'93Tax the Tom Parkers!\'94 chant this scene\'92s floating pig pays off visually. Also draw camp-excess register from \'93Vegas show\'94 (UUID 1DC09FA6) for the wider festival\'92s tone, though that scene\'92s ground-level chaos belongs to Scene 1, not here \'97 this scene stays up on the platform.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 2. Chanta\'92s throne sits empty. Convey this as a fact of the platform\'92s furniture, not a dramatized cutaway \'97 he is not physically present in this scene. A line or aside is enough to place him: carousing with bands and Elvisettes in the green room, avoiding Sarah. Do not stage the green room itself here \'97 that interior belongs to Scene 4 (\'93Chanta\'92s tower\'94), which opens there. Motivational colour (not a new beat, just backstory to draw on): the last real conversation between Sarah and Chanta on a platform like this was at the Inauguration, throne to throne, ending on \'93It\'92s impossible\'94 / \'93Yeah\'94 \'97 verified verbatim against content.rtf (B70CFF1A) \'97 useful for why he can\'92t sit beside her now.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 3. Establish Colonel Tom Porker overhead: a floating pig wearing a cigar and an oversized Stetson \'97 explicitly NOT dressed as Elvis, no jumpsuit. Ties to the established \'93Tax the Tom Parkers!\'94 chant (Inauguration canon, established-facts.md line 241: \'93\'92Tom Parker\'92 invoked as villain archetype... crowd chants \'91Tax the Tom Parkers!\'92 without knowing who he is. Chanta doesn\'92t know who Tom Parker is either.\'94) \'97 the joke made literal and airborne. This is a new visual element, first appearance in the manuscript; nothing to reconcile against, just plant it cleanly.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 4. Sarah on her throne: she came here hoping to vanish into the crowd (consistent with her established pattern \'97 the Vegas Show \'93state of grace\'94/\'94one filament in a never-ending chain,\'94 her chronic wish for anonymity and agency against being handled/watched). She has, again, slipped away from Eloise \'97 \'93a small rebellion, not a scandal,\'94 consistent with her arc of small assertions of control (vaulting the mansion window, refusing invalid treatment; sarah.md).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 5. Eloise arrives silently, just after cocktail hour, having tracked her. Her own office chair \'97 the \'93Ermine Muller\'94 (Herman Miller \'d7 ermine pun) \'97 is brought and set down beside Sarah\'92s throne. She sits. Play the arrival with NO reproach, no cross word: the fact of being found IS the message. This matches both characters\'92 canonical registers under pressure \'97 Eloise\'92s \'93precise, clinical, minimal modifiers\'94 and Sarah\'92s \'93baseline detachment... most world-ending panics arrive smaller than advertised\'94 (both character files). The silence is in character, not a stylistic swerve.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 6. Optional line for Eloise, offered by the author as a possible (not locked) line \'97 unlike the Scene 3 ditty and Scene 1 three laws, which are verbatim and must not be altered, this one may be used, adapted, or dropped: \'93You\'92ll want the aisle seat, in your condition.\'94 Sarah\'92s reaction should be minimal and contained: one flicker she won\'92t let reach her face, then a look back out at the crowd she\'92d come here to vanish into, now that she can\'92t.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 7. Eloise\'92s stated reason for attending is supervising her loaned tanks/hardware (she has loaned military hardware to the Elvi \'97 established-facts.md, eloise.md \'93Calls tanks her \'91loan\'92\'94); the real reason is Sarah. Whether this contrast is voiced on the page (Eloise offering the pretext aloud) or held as authorial/dramatic irony for the reader is open \'97 see below.\
