\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Chanta is not physically present. No cutaway to him or the green room \'97 that\'92s Scene 4\'92s opening territory.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No Sages, no ukuleles, no \'93Praise the Dawkins\'94 ditty here \'97 their entire presence in the sequence is Scene 3, which opens just as the High Elvis is about to go on. This scene should end poised at (or before) that threshold, handing off cleanly.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No Dunhilton/Gerry cutaway (relocated to the later Bent Street scene).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  No floating foetus/idol of any kind \'97 Colonel Tom Porker is the only aerial icon in this scene.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Sarah\'92s pregnancy: by the fixed festival date (Saturday 10 November \'97 timeline.md) and the established conception/birth anchor (conception ~18 March, Christmas birth ~25 Dec \'97 timeline.md line 183), Sarah is roughly third trimester (~34 weeks), materially further along than the \'93barely showing... fifteen weeks\'94 of the Inauguration gown (verified: content.rtf line 1, \'93fifteen weeks now, barely showing\'94). Wardrobe/visual treatment here should reflect a visibly, advancedly pregnant Sarah, not a concealed bump \'97 flagging as a continuity dependency for the drafter rather than prescribing a specific costume.\
