\f1\b0\fs22 \
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Hands off directly into Scene 3: the platform is set, Sarah/Kathy/Hayley/Eloise all seated, the High Elvis about to go on \'97 the Sages\'92 stage invasion follows immediately from where this scene leaves off.\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Plants Sarah\'92s physical tell (hand drifting to belly, flicker she won\'92t let reach her face) that recurs in Scene 5\'92s \'93Religious Minds\'94 cutaway (\'93the baby turns, she keeps her face schooled, her hand betrays her at her belly\'94) \'97 keep the gesture consistent between the two scenes. Precedent verified verbatim: content.rtf (B70CFF1A), \'93Sarah\'92s hand drifted to her belly before she could stop it.\'94\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Establishes Chanta\'92s empty throne and his avoidance of Sarah as the emotional backdrop Scene 4 draws on (his despondency \'93all day\'94 is referenced there).\
\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \uc0\u8226  Introduces two new recurring elements for continuity to log after drafting: Colonel Tom Porker (first appearance, pays off the established Tom Parker chant) and the Ermine Muller chair (new prop tied to Eloise).\
